      "math_academy_id": "q-36288",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "What is the projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8}=-1$ and the plane $y=2$ onto the $xz$-plane?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $y=2$, we substitute $y=2$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+1-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8} & =-2 \\\\ -\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the hyperbola: $-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}=1.$",
